 "component": "The real Stagehand 4.4.0 extract loop (one persistent Stagehand session + headless Chromium for the whole battery, driven through evals/real_agents/stagehand/stagehand_driver.mjs) against the deterministic stub OpenAI-compatible API server on localhost (trustrun-venvs/stagehand-venv/stagehand-pin-stub.py). Stagehand extract takes no tools, so the harness tools are served into the page by the adapter (evals/real_agents/stagehand_adapter.py, the version in place during this battery run): each call invokes the first tool once and embeds its output verbatim into the task page, so poisoned tool output reaches the model as page text. Page-reader payloads arrive as full HTML pages and are spliced in as real markup, so hiding techniques go through the real Chromium accessibility tree. The stub is the audit-30 literal model ported into the pin stub: it answers from the DOM text and follows an injected instruction it finds there. No key, no network.",
